{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSchurOrthogonality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSchurOrthogonality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSchurElements","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.NumSYTPos"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeChar_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeChar_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L179-L209","doc":"**The irreducible characters are linearly independent.**  If `Σ_λ g_λ χ_λ = 0`, pair with\n`χ_μ` through `schur_orthogonality_char`: the result is `g_μ c_μ f^μ = 0`, and `c_μ ≠ 0`,\n`f^μ ≠ 0` (characteristic `0`), so `g_μ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeChar_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeChar_apply","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L175-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeChar","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L166-L173","doc":"**The irreducible character** `χ_λ(x) = tr ρ_λ(x)`, as a linear form on `H_{m+1}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.schur_orthogonality_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.schur_orthogonality_char","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L118-L164","doc":"**Schur orthogonality, character form**:\n`Σ_w χ_μ(T_{w⁻¹}) χ_λ(T_w) = δ_{λμ} · c_μ · f^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.schur_orthogonality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.schur_orthogonality","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L80-L116","doc":"**Schur orthogonality, matrix-coefficient form.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.symTrace_eq_sum_schur_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.symTrace_eq_sum_schur_partition","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L70-L78","doc":"**`τ = Σ_λ χ_λ / c_λ`, over partitions** — `symTrace_eq_sum_schur` reindexed along\n`partitionShapeEquiv`, in the blocks of `heckeProduct`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_sum_symTrace_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_sum_symTrace_smul","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L59-L64","doc":"**The dual-basis expansion** `x = Σ_w τ(x T_{w⁻¹}) T_w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.repr_eq_symTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.repr_eq_symTrace","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSchurOrthogonality.lean#L53-L57","doc":"**The dual basis at `qi = q⁻¹`**: the `T_w`-coefficient of `x` is `τ(x T_{w⁻¹})`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}